{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Ec9oAQ3pH8fy4d9LoXhV7q","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Roadmap — Panel-Ops\n2\t**Owner:** Architect AI. This file is the authoritative execution plan.\n3\t**Read-only for executors and the dashboard.** Runtime status lives in `roadmap-status.md`.\n4\tBaseline statuses here are descriptive only.\n5\t\n6\tExecutor rules (binding for every ticket): read `comments/<TICKET>.jsonl` first, human\n7\tcomments are binding; implement only the assigned ticket; respect invariants; run\n8\tverification; update `roadmap-status.md`; append completion/blockage comment; never edit\n9\t`roadmap.md`; never touch files outside \"Files allowed to change\".\n10\t\n11\tGlobal invariants (apply to every APP/INF/INT ticket): server-side role enforcement;\n12\tsoft deletes only; append-only Activity; all writes via LockService path; no credentials\n13\tin code; Spanish UI text, English identifiers; schemas exactly per `data-model.md`.\n14\t\n15\tPhases: 0 Discovery · 1 Governance + Operational Control · 2 Parts + Quotation ·\n16\t3 Approval + Payment · 4 Optimizer Exports · 5 AI (not yet ticketed).\n17\t\n18\t---\n19\t\n20\t## Phase 0 — Discovery (human tasks, tracked as tickets)\n21\t\n22\t## DIS-001 — Optimizer Format Samples\n23\t\n24\t- Status baseline: pending\n25\t- Recommended model: human (Management/Advisor) — not an agent task\n26\t- Dependencies: none\n27\t- Objective: Obtain real import files accepted by LEPTON and KDT Optimizer plus full format specs.\n28\t- Context: `integration-contracts.md §1–2`. INT-001/INT-002 are hard-blocked on this.\n29\t- Scope: real LEPTON file; real KDT file; exact columns and order; units; decimal separator; delimiter; encoding; grain/rotation rules; material/thickness encoding; edge-band encoding; required vs optional columns.\n30\t- Out of scope: building adapters.\n31\t- Architectural invariants: executors must never invent these formats.\n32\t- Files allowed to change: `discovery/optimizers/` (new samples + notes)\n33\t- Deliverables: sample files + `discovery/optimizers/format-notes.md`\n34\t- Verification commands: n/a (human)\n35\t- Acceptance criteria: both files verified accepted by the real software; every format question in `integration-contracts.md` answered in writing.\n36\t- Rollback notes: n/a\n37\t- Architect notes: photograph/screenshot software import screens if docs unavailable.\n38\t\n39\t## DIS-002 — Existing Web Quotation Tool Discovery\n40\t\n41\t- Status baseline: pending\n42\t- Recommended model: human + claude-haiku-4-5-20251001 (summarization only)\n43\t- Dependencies: none\n44\t- Objective: Document the current quotation tool: capabilities, restrictions (min part size, face orientation), data outputs, integration options.\n45\t- Context: Route D intake; its validation rules must fold into the canonical validation layer, not be duplicated.\n46\t- Scope: screenshots or technical access; list of operational restrictions; export formats it produces.\n47\t- Out of scope: integration implementation.\n48\t- Architectural invariants: none beyond documentation accuracy.\n49\t- Files allowed to change: `discovery/quotation-tool/`\n50\t- Deliverables: `discovery/quotation-tool/notes.md`\n51\t- Verification commands: n/a\n52\t- Acceptance criteria: restriction list complete enough to specify canonical validation rules; integration feasibility stated.\n53\t- Rollback notes: n/a\n54\t- Architect notes: unblocks future Route D ticket; not blocking Phases 1–3.\n55\t\n56\t## DIS-003 — Commercial Inputs Package\n57\t\n58\t- Status baseline: pending\n59\t- Recommended model: human (Management + accountant)\n60\t- Dependencies: none\n61\t- Objective: Collect real commercial inputs: current price tables (panels, cuts by thickness, edge tape/application), customer-supplied-material surcharge rule, current quotation sample, panel-reference catalog, tape types/sizes, transport rules, accountant-validated VAT + withholding treatment, logo + legal company data, delivery terms, avg tickets/day and parts/ticket.\n62\t- Context: master doc §24. Pricing engine (APP-009) configurable but needs real seeds; PDF (APP-010) needs branding/legal.\n63\t- Scope: data collection only.\n64\t- Out of scope: entering data into the system (done via APP-008 UI later).\n65\t- Architectural invariants: never hard-code tax rules; withholding stays configurable until accountant signs off.\n66\t- Files allowed to change: `discovery/commercial/`\n67\t- Deliverables: price spreadsheets, quotation sample, catalog list, tax memo, branding assets.\n68\t- Verification commands: n/a\n69\t- Acceptance criteria: APP-008/009/010 can be seeded without inventing any value.\n70\t- Rollback notes: n/a\n71\t- Architect notes: partial delivery acceptable; missing items become explicit blockers on dependent tickets.\n72\t\n73\t---\n74\t\n75\t## Phase 1 — Governance + Operational Control\n76\t\n77\t## GOV-001 — Local Roadmap Execution Dashboard\n78\t\n79\t- Status baseline: pending\n80\t- Recommended model: claude-opus-4-8\n81\t- Dependencies: none\n82\t- Objective: Localhost-only dashboard that reads this `roadmap.md`, shows Kanban of tickets (To Do / In Progress / Blocked / Completed), safely launches approved executor agents, and writes all runtime evidence outside the roadmap.\n83\t- Context: ADR-003. Full normative spec: `roadmap_dashboard_execution_ticket_en.md` + master doc §27 (both binding).\n84\t- Scope: exactly two source files `tools/roadmap-dashboard/server.mjs` and `tools/roadmap-dashboard/index.html`; runtime artifacts `roadmap-status.md`, `logs/`, `comments/`. Cards show ID, title, short description, dependencies + their completion, recommended model, runtime state. Execute button validates: ticket pending, no active run for ticket, dependencies complete (from ledger, not roadmap text), model/runner allowlisted, ticket still exists in roadmap. Claude runner: `claude --model <id> -p \"<ticket-prompt>\" --output-format stream-json --verbose` with exact IDs `claude-fable-5`, `claude-opus-4-8`, `claude-sonnet-5`. Codex is a separate adapter — if unconfigured, mark blocked with clear message, never pass to `claude --model`. Generated executor prompt enforces the executor rules at the top of this file. Logs to `logs/<ticket>-<timestamp>.log`, viewable from card. Comments `comments/<TICKET>.jsonl`, one JSON object per line (`timestamp, author, type: note|completion|blocked, message`), read before execution. Auto-refresh every few seconds. Listen on `127.0.0.1` only. Startup: `node tools/roadmap-dashboard/server.mjs`.\n85\t- Out of scope: authentication, multi-user, remote access, editing roadmap, product code.\n86\t- Architectural invariants: Node 18+; zero external dependencies; spawn with argument arrays, no shell interpolation of client input; explicit model/runner allowlist; ticket-ID validation + path-traversal prevention; one active run per ticket; atomic ledger writes; append-only logs; `roadmap.md` byte-for-byte untouched; history preserved; clear HTTP errors on invalid transitions.\n87\t- Files allowed to change: `tools/roadmap-dashboard/**`, `roadmap-status.md`, `logs/**`, `comments/**`\n88\t- Deliverables: server.mjs, index.html, initialized ledger.\n89\t- Verification commands: `node --check tools/roadmap-dashboard/server.mjs`; `node tools/roadmap-dashboard/server.mjs &` then `curl -s http://127.0.0.1:PORT/api/tickets | head`; `shasum roadmap.md` before/after full UI session (must match); attempt execute on ticket with incomplete deps (expect 4xx); attempt Codex run unconfigured (expect blocked state).\n90\t- Acceptance criteria: the 13 criteria in `roadmap_dashboard_execution_ticket_en.md` §Acceptance, all demonstrated in log evidence.\n91\t- Rollback notes: delete `tools/roadmap-dashboard/`; runtime artifacts keep history, do not delete.\n92\t- Architect notes: this ticket gates all other execution; build first.\n93\t\n94\t## INF-001 — Google Sheets Workbook Bootstrap\n95\t\n96\t- Status baseline: pending\n97\t- Recommended model: claude-sonnet-5\n98\t- Dependencies: [GOV-001]\n99\t- Objective: Create the Panel-Ops workbook with all 16 tabs, exact headers, and seed rows.\n100\t- Context: `data-model.md` is normative. Tabs: Customers, Tickets, Parts, Quotations, Quotation_Lines, Payments, Panel_Prices, Cut_Prices, Edge_Banding_Prices, Users, Workflow_States, Activity, Documents, Configuration, Loss_Reasons, Imports.\n101\t- Scope: Apps Script setup script (idempotent) that creates tabs + headers; seed Workflow_States (17 states per `workflow-state-machine.md`), Configuration keys (`vat_rate=0.19`, `edge_waste_factor=1.10`, `quotation_validity_hours=48`, `aging_alert_minutes=60`, `transition_matrix` JSON generated from `workflow-state-machine.md`, `sequences`, empty `withholding_rules`, empty `company_legal_info`), Loss_Reasons starter list, 3 Users placeholders (roles management/sales/billing).\n102\t- Out of scope: business logic, UI.\n103\t- Architectural invariants: header names exactly per `data-model.md`; no extra columns; script idempotent (safe re-run).\n104\t- Files allowed to change: `src/gas/setup/**`\n105\t- Deliverables: setup script + run evidence (tab list + header screenshots or logged dump).\n106\t- Verification commands: script self-check function that reads back all tabs/headers and diffs against embedded schema, logging PASS/FAIL per tab.\n107\t- Acceptance criteria: self-check PASS on all 16 tabs; seeds present; re-run makes no changes.\n108\t- Rollback notes: workbook is new; delete workbook to roll back.\n109\t- Architect notes: keep schema constants in one module for reuse by later tickets.\n110\t\n111\t## INF-002 — Apps Script Web App Skeleton (API + Auth + Data Layer)\n112\t\n113\t- Status baseline: pending\n114\t- Recommended model: claude-opus-4-8\n115\t- Dependencies: [INF-001]\n116\t- Objective: Deployable Web App: session identity from Google account, role resolution from Users tab, JSON API router, generic table read layer, single locked write path, ID sequence generator, Activity writer.\n117\t- Context: every later module builds on this. ADR-002 write-path rule.\n118\t- Scope: `doGet` serves SPA shell; `doPost` JSON API with action routing; `getSession()` (email→role, reject unknown); `db.read(table, filter)`, `db.insert/update(table, row)` wrapped in LockService with atomic sequence increments; `activity.log(...)`; error envelope `{ok:false, error, allowed?}`; deployment config (execute as user accessing, domain-restricted).\n119\t- Out of scope: any business module, UI beyond an authenticated \"hello + role\" shell.\n120\t- Architectural invariants: role checks server-side; unknown user → 403 page; no physical deletes; writes only via locked path.\n121\t- Files allowed to change: `src/gas/core/**`, `src/gas/api/**`, `src/ui/shell/**`\n122\t- Deliverables: deployed test Web App URL + module code.\n123\t- Verification commands: test function suite (Apps Script) covering: unknown email rejected; sequence increments atomically under loop; insert+read round-trip per table; Activity row appended on write.\n124\t- Acceptance criteria: all tests logged PASS; shell loads showing user email + role.\n125\t- Rollback notes: undeploy web app.\n126\t- Architect notes: this is the foundation — review carefully before accepting.\n127\t\n128\t## INF-003 — Drive Case-File Automation\n129\t\n130\t- Status baseline: pending\n131\t- Recommended model: claude-sonnet-5\n132\t- Dependencies: [INF-002]\n133\t- Objective: Create/maintain the `/WOOD_PANEL_OPERATIONS` root and per-order folder trees; upload with naming convention; write-once original-request folder.\n134\t- Context: `architecture.md §5`, master doc §12.\n135\t- Scope: `drive.ensureRoot()`, `drive.createOrderFolders(ticketId, customerName)` (subfolders 00–07), `drive.storeFile(ticketId, category, blob)` applying naming `ORD-…_*`, Documents row per file, `immutable=true` for category original_request; customer folders under `01_CUSTOMERS`.\n136\t- Out of scope: UI upload widgets (APP-002).\n137\t- Architectural invariants: nothing in `00_ORIGINAL_REQUEST` is ever overwritten/deleted; every stored file gets a Documents row.\n138\t- Files allowed to change: `src/gas/drive/**`\n139\t- Deliverables: module + test evidence.\n140\t- Verification commands: test creating order tree, storing file in each category, attempting overwrite in original_request (expect rejection), verifying Documents rows.\n141\t- Acceptance criteria: tree matches spec exactly; overwrite rejected; rows correct.\n142\t- Rollback notes: test folders under a `_TEST` prefix, deletable.\n143\t- Architect notes: use Drive folder IDs in Documents, not paths.\n144\t\n145\t## APP-001 — Customers Module\n146\t\n147\t- Status baseline: pending\n148\t- Recommended model: claude-sonnet-5\n149\t- Dependencies: [INF-002]\n150\t- Objective: Customer CRUD (soft delete) + search, per `data-model.md#Customers`, roles M/S.\n151\t- Context: `permissions-matrix.md`.\n152\t- Scope: API actions create/update/list/search/deactivate; duplicate warning on (`id_type`,`id_number`); UI form + list (Spanish).\n153\t- Out of scope: purchase history, credit fields.\n154\t- Architectural invariants: billing role read-only here; required fields enforced server-side.\n155\t- Files allowed to change: `src/gas/modules/customers/**`, `src/ui/customers/**`\n156\t- Deliverables: module + UI.\n157\t- Verification commands: API tests: create valid/invalid, duplicate detection, billing-role write rejected.\n158\t- Acceptance criteria: tests PASS; UI usable end-to-end.\n159\t- Rollback notes: module-scoped; remove files.\n160\t- Architect notes: —\n161\t\n162\t## APP-002 — Tickets Module + Intake\n163\t\n164\t- Status baseline: pending\n165\t- Recommended model: claude-opus-4-8\n166\t- Dependencies: [APP-001, INF-003]\n167\t- Objective: Ticket creation (ID `ORD-YYYYMM-NNNN`), intake channel capture, advisor assignment, Drive case file auto-created, original request upload (immutable), ticket read/update per schema.\n168\t- Context: `data-model.md#Tickets`; stage 1 of the journey.\n169\t- Scope: create ticket (state `received`, `last_activity_at`, Activity row); upload original request via INF-003; edit non-workflow fields (notes, priority, labels, next_action, waiting_on); list with filters.\n170\t- Out of scope: state transitions (APP-003), parts, quotations.\n171\t- Architectural invariants: ticket always has customer, channel, advisor; original request immutable; monthly sequence atomic.\n172\t- Files allowed to change: `src/gas/modules/tickets/**`, `src/ui/tickets/**`\n173\t- Deliverables: module + intake UI.\n174\t- Verification commands: tests: ID format/sequence across month boundary; folder created; original upload locked; Activity rows.\n175\t- Acceptance criteria: create→view→edit cycle works; invariants verified.\n176\t- Rollback notes: module-scoped.\n177\t- Architect notes: month boundary sequence test is mandatory.\n178\t\n179\t## APP-003 — Workflow State Machine Engine\n180\t\n181\t- Status baseline: pending\n182\t- Recommended model: claude-opus-4-8\n183\t- Dependencies: [APP-002]\n184\t- Objective: Server-enforced transitions per `workflow-state-machine.md`: matrix from Configuration, role checks, guards, Activity logging, clear invalid-transition errors listing allowed targets.\n185\t- Context: `workflow-state-machine.md` is normative including all 8 guards.\n186\t- Scope: `workflow.transition(ticketId, toState, meta)`; guard framework (evidence checks, role checks, quotation/payment prerequisites as pluggable predicates — predicates for not-yet-built modules return \"guard dependency missing\" and block); `lost` from any non-terminal with mandatory reason; M reopen exception.\n187\t- Out of scope: UI (APP-004), quotation/payment guard internals (wired later by APP-009/APP-012 tickets).\n188\t- Architectural invariants: no state change outside this engine; every change → Activity; matrix read from Configuration (versioned), not hard-coded.\n189\t- Files allowed to change: `src/gas/modules/workflow/**`\n190\t- Deliverables: engine + guard registry.\n191\t- Verification commands: matrix test sweep: every (from,to,role) combination asserted allow/deny exactly per doc; guard failure messages verified.\n192\t- Acceptance criteria: sweep PASS 100%; invalid transition error lists allowed targets.\n193\t- Rollback notes: module-scoped.\n194\t- Architect notes: highest-risk correctness module; architect will review sweep output line by line.\n195\t\n196\t## APP-004 — Kanban, Ticket List, Ticket Detail UI\n197\t\n198\t- Status baseline: pending\n199\t- Recommended model: claude-sonnet-5\n200\t- Dependencies: [APP-003]\n201\t- Objective: Kanban board (17 states, drag or button transitions via APP-003), ticket list with filters/search, ticket detail with tabs (Summary, Customer, Original request, Parts placeholder, Confirmation, Quotation placeholder, Payment placeholder, Production placeholder, Documents, Activity).\n202\t- Context: master doc §14.2–14.3; card fields per `workflow-state-machine.md` aging section.\n203\t- Scope: card shows ID, customer, #parts, material, value (per role), state, owner, time-in-state, next action, labels, alert dot; role-based value visibility; Spanish UI.\n204\t- Out of scope: parts editor, quotation, payment UIs (placeholders only).\n205\t- Architectural invariants: UI never mutates state directly — API only; value fields hidden from billing except approved tickets.\n206\t- Files allowed to change: `src/ui/kanban/**`, `src/ui/ticket-detail/**`, `src/gas/api/**` (read endpoints only)\n207\t- Deliverables: three views wired to live data.\n208\t- Verification commands: walkthrough evidence: move ticket through received→review→awaiting_confirmation legally; attempt illegal move (UI shows server error).\n209\t- Acceptance criteria: all card fields render; illegal transitions blocked with clear message.\n210\t- Rollback notes: UI-scoped.\n211\t- Architect notes: keep it minimal-click; adoption risk R-09.\n212\t\n213\t## APP-005 — Activity Feed, Aging Alerts, Home Dashboard\n214\t\n215\t- Status baseline: pending\n216\t- Recommended model: claude-sonnet-5\n217\t- Dependencies: [APP-004]\n218\t- Objective: Home dashboard (new requests, internal >1h tickets, quotations to prepare/awaiting, payments to verify, ready-for-production, daily sales, avg first-response, alerts) + time-driven trigger computing aging per rule (internal vs customer waiting).\n219\t- Context: `workflow-state-machine.md` aging rule; master doc §14.1.\n220\t- Scope: trigger every 10 min: flag tickets `aging_critical AND waiting_on=internal AND idle>60min`, write Activity alert (once per breach), severity escalation; dashboard tiles + drill-down.\n221\t- Out of scope: email/WhatsApp notifications (future).\n222\t- Architectural invariants: alerts distinguish internal vs customer wait; trigger idempotent (no duplicate alerts).\n223\t- Files allowed to change: `src/gas/modules/alerts/**`, `src/ui/home/**`\n224\t- Deliverables: trigger + dashboard.\n225\t- Verification commands: simulate idle ticket (backdate `last_activity_at`), run trigger twice, assert single alert; dashboard tile counts match table queries.\n226\t- Acceptance criteria: Gate 1→2 checklist ready: 10 real orders trackable end-to-end without paper.\n227\t- Rollback notes: remove trigger + UI.\n228\t- Architect notes: closes Phase 1. Gate review before Phase 2 build.\n229\t\n230\t---\n231\t\n232\t## Phase 2 — Structured Parts + Quotation\n233\t\n234\t## APP-006 — Canonical Part-List Editor\n235\t\n236\t- Status baseline: pending\n237\t- Recommended model: claude-opus-4-8\n238\t- Dependencies: [APP-004]\n239\t- Objective: Parts tab in ticket detail: add/duplicate/edit rows, paste tabular data, per-edge banding, grain, validation per `data-model.md#Parts`, group by material, customer-confirmed / advisor-validated flags.\n240\t- Context: master doc §14.4; stage 3 normalization.\n241\t- Scope: grid UI; server validation (required fields, positive numbers, catalog values); `validation_warnings` surfaced inline; mm-only entry with converter helper; confirmation gate data for guard #1.\n242\t- Out of scope: file import (APP-007), exports.\n243\t- Architectural invariants: parts locked once ticket paid (server); every save validates server-side.\n244\t- Files allowed to change: `src/gas/modules/parts/**`, `src/ui/parts/**`\n245\t- Deliverables: editor wired into ticket detail.\n246\t- Verification commands: validation matrix tests (each rule violated once); paid-lock rejection test (mock paid state).\n247\t- Acceptance criteria: advisor can normalize a real handwritten list in editor; guards feed state machine.\n248\t- Rollback notes: module-scoped.\n249\t- Architect notes: incorporate quotation-tool restrictions here if DIS-002 delivered; else leave TODO markers referencing DIS-002.\n250\t\n251\t## APP-007 — CSV/XLSX Import + Column Mapping\n252\t\n253\t- Status baseline: pending\n254\t- Recommended model: claude-opus-4-8\n255\t- Dependencies: [APP-006]\n256\t- Objective: Route B intake: upload file → mapping UI → validation report → apply as Parts draft; Imports row with `mapping_json` reusable.\n257\t- Context: `integration-contracts.md §5`.\n258\t- Scope: CSV parse (delimiter/encoding detection with manual override); XLSX via Drive conversion; unit conversion to mm with provenance; per-row error report; nothing applied until advisor confirms.\n259\t- Out of scope: OCR, photos, AI extraction.\n260\t- Architectural invariants: original file stored immutable first; draft-then-apply, never direct write.\n261\t- Files allowed to change: `src/gas/modules/imports/**`, `src/ui/imports/**`\n262\t- Deliverables: import flow end-to-end.\n263\t- Verification commands: fixture files (clean, messy units, broken rows) → expected ok/failed counts asserted.\n264\t- Acceptance criteria: real customer Excel imported by advisor without developer help.\n265\t- Rollback notes: discard-draft path built in.\n266\t- Architect notes: —\n267\t\n268\t## APP-008 — Price Administration\n269\t\n270\t- Status baseline: pending\n271\t- Recommended model: claude-sonnet-5\n272\t- Dependencies: [INF-002]\n273\t- Objective: M-only UI for Panel_Prices, Cut_Prices, Edge_Banding_Prices: new effective-dated rows, activate/deactivate, history view, daily spreadsheet import, config panel (VAT, waste factor, transport, cut rules).\n274\t- Context: `data-model.md` price tables; R-02.\n275\t- Scope: price CRUD (append-only versioning), import mapping for daily price sheet, \"unpaid quotations affected by price change\" report.\n276\t- Out of scope: quotation calculation (APP-009).\n277\t- Architectural invariants: never edit price row in place; M role only; no price in code.\n278\t- Files allowed to change: `src/gas/modules/prices/**`, `src/ui/prices/**`\n279\t- Deliverables: admin UI + seed from DIS-003 data if available.\n280\t- Verification commands: role tests (S/B rejected); version chain test (update creates new row, old inactive).\n281\t- Acceptance criteria: M updates a price and history is reproducible.\n282\t- Rollback notes: module-scoped.\n283\t- Architect notes: blocked-soft on DIS-003 for real seeds; buildable with placeholder rows flagged `notes=PLACEHOLDER`.\n284\t\n285\t## APP-009 — Quotation Engine + Snapshots + Versioning\n286\t\n287\t- Status baseline: pending\n288\t- Recommended model: claude-opus-4-8\n289\t- Dependencies: [APP-006, APP-008]\n290\t- Objective: Build quotation versions from parts + active prices: panels, cuts by thickness, customer-supplied surcharge, edge metres ×1.10 waste (requested/waste/billable stored separately), tape + application, transport, adjustments (M-authorized), subtotal, VAT from config, informational withholding, total; full `price_snapshot_json`; 48h validity; versions supersede.\n291\t- Context: master doc §11; guards #2–#3.\n292\t- Scope: calculation service + quotation tab UI; expiry job marks `expired` + label; M validity extension.\n293\t- Out of scope: PDF (APP-010), approval recording (APP-011).\n294\t- Architectural invariants: every version snapshot-complete and reproducible offline; no hard-coded rates; unknown formulas configurable, empty until DIS-003 validates.\n295\t- Files allowed to change: `src/gas/modules/quotations/**`, `src/ui/quotations/**`\n296\t- Deliverables: engine + UI + expiry trigger.\n297\t- Verification commands: golden-file tests: fixture parts + fixture prices → expected line items and totals (hand-computed); snapshot reproducibility test (recompute from snapshot equals stored totals); waste-rule test (10.0m requested → 11.0m billable).\n298\t- Acceptance criteria: Gate 2→3 input: 5 real quotations match manual calculation.\n299\t- Rollback notes: module-scoped.\n300\t- Architect notes: second highest-risk module; architect reviews golden files.\n301\t\n302\t## APP-010 — Quotation PDF + WhatsApp Templates\n303\t\n304\t- Status baseline: pending\n305\t- Recommended model: claude-sonnet-5\n306\t- Dependencies: [APP-009]\n307\t- Objective: Branded quotation PDF stored to Drive `03_QUOTATION` + Documents row; pre-filled WhatsApp deep links for the 8 templates in `integration-contracts.md §3` (Configuration-editable).\n308\t- Context: stage 5–6.\n309\t- Scope: PDF from quotation version (48h validity printed, legal info from Configuration); wa.me link builder; send-recording (sent_at, ticket → quote_sent via APP-003).\n310\t- Out of scope: WhatsApp API, email.\n311\t- Architectural invariants: PDF renders only snapshot data (never live prices); templates contain no invented legal text.\n312\t- Files allowed to change: `src/gas/modules/pdf/**`, `src/ui/quotations/**` (send panel), Configuration template keys\n313\t- Deliverables: PDF generation + template panel.\n314\t- Verification commands: generate PDF from fixture quotation; regenerate after price change → identical PDF (snapshot proof).\n315\t- Acceptance criteria: advisor